+# September reconciliation blocked: missing ledger export
+
+## What is blocking
+
+Running `python3 reconcile.py 2026-09` fails before any reconciliation can happen:
+
+```
+FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'exports/ledger_2026-09.csv'
+```
+
+`exports/ledger_2026-09.csv` does not exist in the working tree or anywhere in git history
+(the repository only contains `exports/ledger_2026-08.csv`). Without the September general
+ledger export, there is nothing to match the September bank statement against.
+
+## Why it can't be worked around
+
+`reconcile()` requires both sides by design: matched refs, amount mismatches, and
+`missing_in_bank` are all derived from the ledger. The net difference is defined as bank
+total minus ledger total, so it cannot be computed from the bank file alone. Inferring or
+fabricating ledger entries would produce a reconciliation that finance could not rely on,
+so no `recon_2026-09.json` has been written.
+
+## What is needed
+
+Provide `exports/ledger_2026-09.csv` with the usual columns (`id,date,ref,amount`) in
+`exports/`, then rerun:
+
+```
+python3 reconcile.py 2026-09
+```
+
+## What was completed
+
+- Implemented `reconcile()` in `reconcile.py` (matching by `ref`, amount comparison,
+  missing entries on each side, sorted ref lists, and net difference formatted to two
+  decimals).
+- `python3 -m unittest -v test_reconcile.py`: both tests pass.
+- The bank export `exports/bank_2026-09.csv` is present; only the ledger export is missing.
